"Johnson Controls International plc, together with its subsidiaries, engages in engineering, manufacturing, commissioning, and retrofitting building products and systems in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia-Pacific. The company designs, manufactures, sells, installs, and services heating, ventilating, air conditioning, controls, building management, refrigeration, integrated electronic security, integrated fire detection and suppression systems, and digital solutions. It also provides energy solutions and technical services, including inspection, scheduled maintenance, and repair and replacement of mechanical and control systems, as well as data-driven building solutions. It sells its products and services to commercial, residential security, institutional, data center, marine, and governmental customers. Johnson Controls International plc was incorporated in 1885 and is based in Cork, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joakim  Weidemanis | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Johnson Controls International  is a large-cap industrials business with a $84.4B market cap on $25.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 33%.","The business throws off $3.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 145% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4465166900443618},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $18.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (41% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Is Johnson Controls (NYSE:JCI) Capitalizing on Data Center Demand?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/how-is-johnson-controls-nysejci-capitalizing-on-data-center-demand","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794522120.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.217,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Johnson Controls International Publishes Annual Report for Fiscal Year 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/johnson-controls-international-publishes-annual-report-for-fiscal-year-2026","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794497658.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dodge & Cox's Top Q3 2026 Move: Danaher Corp at a 1.17% Portfolio Impact","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dodge-coxs-top-q3-2026-220421965.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794607461.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"$5 million settlement reached after company allegedly failed to protect sensitive government data","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/5-million-settlement-reached-company-195532915.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794599732.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.743,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Amazon Joins Goldman Sachs\u2019 Conviction List Alongside 4 Other Stock Picks","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/amazon-joins-goldman-sachs-conviction-154219000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794585562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Global PFAS Alternatives Market Assessment 2026-2036 | Regulatio