ctor operating profit.","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-2.6% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.01 across 548 companies in the universe; the top four hold 9% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 31% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 6% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 13% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 33% and a beta of 1.04, it moves roughly with the market.","Liquidity is deep, with about $464.8M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 44% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 67% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $56.95 (margin of safety -145%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 28%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $40.78 to $79.97 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: EV/EBITDA 20.3 vs 13.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 46% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.0% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 21 covering analysts target $174 on average, 25% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.3%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.73).","It runs a 33% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.36x.","ROE of 21% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.9x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 5pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.0% of revenue on R&D and 0.5% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.8x net debt to EBITDA ($618.0M of cash against $8.2B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 16.4x.","The current ratio of 0.90 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Goodwill makes up 41% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -1.4% over 3 years, 1.6% over 5 years and -3.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 68%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 11.3% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.3% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.26 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 1.1x annual revenue and deferred revenue up 36%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (1.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and institutions hold 92%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $18.1M sold).","It returns 2.9% a year to shareholders (1.8% in buybacks and 1.1% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 3.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 38 consecutive years, raising it 5.1% a year over the last five."],"people":["CEO pay is $4.0M."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":45,"head":"Avoid: priced 145% above its fair value of $56.95.","pros":["FCF margin 13.3%","21 analysts' mean target $174 (+25%)","12-1 month momentum +31%","Operating margin expanding 1.3%/yr"],"cons":["Trades 145% above fair value of $56.95","ROIC 8.7% vs WACC 9.3%","EV/EBITDA 20.3x vs sector 13.4x"],"flags":["Priced 145% above its fair value of $56.95"],"need":[],"buy_below":48.41,"vc":{"base":56.95,"base_src":"dcf","bear":40.78,"bull":79.97,"alt_median":29.67,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.9193,"dispersion":0.2832,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 92% above the other mode